HA}\\` constants + \\`EncodeSkills\\`/\\`DecodeSkills\\` helpers.\n- Lifecycle \\`UserPromptSubmit\\` hook now reads env vars via new \\`adoptReviewEnv\\`; old marker-adoption path (\\`adoptPendingReviewMarkerInto\\`, \\`sameWorktreePath\\`) deleted from the lifecycle.\n- Pinned JSON wire format for \\`Kind\\`, \\`ReviewSkills\\`, \\`ReviewPrompt\\` on \\`CommittedMetadata\\` and \\`HasReview\\` on \\`CheckpointSummary\\`.\n- Net diff: **+434 / −472** (deletes more than adds).\n\n**CU2 — AgentReviewer interface + Process + Event types** (\\`c4b7bced3\\`)\n- New \\`cmd/entire/cli/review/types/reviewer.go\\` defines:\n  - \\`AgentReviewer\\` (per-agent contract: \\`Name() string\\`, \\`Start(ctx, RunConfig) (Process, error)\\`)\n  - \\`Process\\` (\\`Events() <-chan Event\\`, \\`Wait() error\\`)\n  - \\`RunConfig\\` (Skills, AlwaysPrompt, PerRunPrompt, ScopeBaseRef, StartingSHA)\n  - \\`Event\\` sealed sum type: \\`Started\\`, \\`AssistantText\\`, \\`ToolCall\\`, \\`Tokens{In,Out}\\`, \\`Finished{Success}\\`, \\`RunError{Err}\\`\n- Pure types — no implementations. Implementations land in PR-A2.\n- Net diff: **+228 / 0**.\n\n## Why env-var handshake\n\nEach spawned agent inherits its own env, so multiple worktrees and multi-agent runs are correct by construction. Eliminates four bug classes from the prior design:\n- Worktree race on shared marker file (was [issue from PR #993])\n- Empty \\`ReviewSkills\\` on multi-agent runs (HIGH-severity Bugbot finding from PR #1018)\n- Marker overwrite tripwire (no longer needed)\n- Refuse-attach-when-checkpoint-missing guard (no longer needed)\n\n## Architectural notes\n\n- \\`review/types/\\` lives in a subpackage to break import cycles between per-agent reviewer packages (PR-A2) and the orchestrator (PR-A2). Both depend on this leaf package; neither depends on the other.\n- \\`Event\\` is sealed via private \\`isEvent()\\` method — adding a variant requires editing this file (intentional contract change).\n- \\`Process.Wait\\` contract is explicit: \\`nil\\` on clean exit, \\`ctx.Err()\\` on cancel, \\`*exec.ExitError\\` on non-zero, other types for I/O failures. Documented at the interface so consumers can use \\`errors.As\\`/\\`errors.Is\\`.\n- \\`Sink\\` (will land in A2) commits to **serial-dispatch concurrency** — orchestrator serializes calls even under multi-agent runs (PR-B's RunMulti fans events from N agents into one dispatch loop). Sinks need not internally synchronize.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- [x] \\`mise run check\\` (fmt + lint + test:ci) green\n- [x] Per-package unit tests pass: \\`go test ./cmd/entire/cli/review/ ./cmd/entire/cli/review/types/ ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/ ./cmd/entire/cli/\\`\n- [x] Integration test \\`TestReview_EnvVarAdoptionCondensesReviewMetadataOnNextCommit\\` covers the full flow (env set → hook subprocess → state tagged → commit → checkpoint metadata)\n\n## Smoke test (env-handshake against real binary)\n\nEnd-to-end verification that env-var handshake works on a real binary in a real repo. Procedure:\n\n\\`\\`\\`bash\ngit checkout feat/entire-review-v2-a1\ngo build -o /tmp/entire-smoke-a1 ./cmd/entire\n\n# Set up a fresh test repo\nrm -rf /tmp/smoke-a1 && mkdir /tmp/smoke-a1 && cd /tmp/smoke-a1\ngit init -q && git config user.email a@b.c && git config user.name x\necho init > README.md && git add . && git commit -q -m init\n/tmp/entire-smoke-a1 enable --agent claude-code --local\n\n# Invoke the lifecycle hook with ENTIRE_REVIEW_* set\necho '{\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"smoke-a1\\\",\\\"prompt\\\":\\\"x\\\"}' | \\\\\n  ENTIRE_REVIEW_SESSION=1 \\\\\n  ENTIRE_REVIEW_AGENT=claude-code \\\\\n  ENTIRE_REVIEW_SKILLS='[\\\"/test\\\"]' \\\\\n  ENTIRE_REVIEW_PROMPT=x \\\\\n  ENTIRE_REVIEW_STARTING_SHA=\\\"\\$(git rev-parse HEAD)\\\" \\\\\n  /tmp/entire-smoke-a1 hooks claude-code user-prompt-submit\n\n# Verify session state is tagged as a review\ncat .git/entire-sessions/smoke-a1.json | jq '.kind, .review_skills, .review_prompt'\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n**Expected output:**\n\\`\\`\\`\n\\\"agent_review\\\"\n[\\\"/test\\\"]\n\\\"x\\\"\n\\`\\`\\`\n\n**Actual output (verified locally on \\`feat/entire-review-v2-a1\\` @ c4b7bced3):**\n\\`\\`\\`\n\\\"agent_review\\\"\n[\\\"/test\\\"]\n\\\"x\\\"\n\\`\\`\\`\n✓ Env handshake works end-to-end on the real binary.\n\n## Anti-features explicitly NOT recreated (do not reintroduce)\n\n- \\`PendingReviewMarker\\` adoption from the lifecycle hook (env handshake replaces it)\n- \\`WorktreePath\\` field + worktree-scoping fallback logic\n- \\`AgentEntries\\` map on the marker\n- Marker overwrite tripwire / refuse-attach guard\n\n(Note: \\`PendingReviewMarker\\` write/read remains in old \\`review.go\\` for non-launchable agents — that's CU6/PR-A3's removal scope.)\n\n<!-- CURSOR_SUMMARY -->\n---\n\n> [!NOTE]\n> **Medium Risk**\n> Changes how review sessions are tagged by switching lifecycle adoption from a shared on-disk marker file to process env vars, which could affect review metadata persistence if misconfigured. Adds new review orchestration type contracts but no implementations yet, so runtime impact is mainly in lifecycle/session-state handling and its tests.\n> \n> **Overview**\n> Switches review-session adoption from a shared `.git/entire-sessions/review-pending.json` marker to an **env-var handshake**: lifecycle turn start now reads `ENTIRE_REVIEW_*` (new `review/env.go`) to tag a session as `agent_review` and persist `ReviewSkills`/`ReviewPrompt`, removing the marker adoption logic and related test helpers.\n> \n> Adds new foundational interfaces/types for the upcoming `entire review` rewrite (`review/types`: `AgentReviewer`, `Process`, sealed `Event` taxonomy, `RunConfig`) and updates integration/unit tests to simulate the env-based flow. Also adds checkpoint tests that pin the on-disk JSON key names for review-related fields (`CommittedMetadata` review fields and `CheckpointSummary.has_review`).\n> \n> <sup>Reviewed by [Cursor Bugbot](https://cursor.com/bugbot) for commit 37f5f0f431c5c96e7c2be3b3